Trust (TR). The importance of trust has been confirmed in different domains, especially in the adoption of new technologies [70]. It is suggested that trust may explain the individual acceptance of driving assistance systems [72]. In addition, trust is a major determinant of reliance on and acceptance of automation technology, standing between people’s beliefs toward automation and their intention to use it [73,74]. In line with previous research, it was demonstrated that trust exhibited strong direct effects on intention to use (H6(c), β = 0.179, p = 0.019) and indirect impacts on intention to use through perceived usefulness (H6(a), β = 0.246, p < 0.001) and attitude (H6(b), β = 0.143, p = 0.03).

